 Top 8 NGINX Use Cases 🔥

NGINX is much more than a web server - it's the backbone of high-performance applications.
Here's where it shines 👇

🔄 Reverse Proxy -> Hide backend servers and route client requests.

⚖️ Load Balancer -> Distribute traffic across multiple servers.

📂 Static File Server -> Serve HTML, CSS, JS, and images at lightning speed.

🔐 TLS Termination -> Offload SSL/TLS encryption for better performance.

⚡ Caching Layer -> Cache responses to reduce latency and backend load.

🚦 Rate Limiting -> Protect APIs from abuse and DDoS attacks.

🛣️ Request Routing -> Route traffic based on URL, domain, or headers.

🔌 WebSocket Proxy -> Enable real-time communication for chats, gaming, and live apps.

👉🏻 Quick Takeaway:

If you're building scalable web applications or APIs, NGINX is one of the most powerful tools in your infrastructure stack.
